# Shared drawing operations. A host owns the shader resource and its GPU buffers.
import view.dl
import shader_types.dl
import shader_values.dl

to get [the UI shader operations in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set provider to view's driver's shader operations
    require condition (provider != @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI shader operations)) reporting "This platform has no shader program provider"
    return provider

to get [a UI texture from shader] {a pointer:shader} [sized] {integer:width} [by] {integer:height} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    set {pixel width} to a UI operation integer from width
    set {pixel height} to a UI operation integer from height
    require condition ((pixel width > 0) and (pixel height > 0)) reporting "Shader texture dimensions must be positive"
    set resource to @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's frame, a pointer, view, shader, pixel width, pixel height)
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI texture, resource, pixel width, pixel height)

to [set UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [uniform group] {integer:group} [binding] {integer:binding} [to] {UI shader value:value}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    require UI shader type storing (value's scalar) with (value's rows) rows and (value's columns) columns
    @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's uniforms, nothing, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass, a UI operation integer from group, a UI operation integer from binding, value's scalar, value's rows, value's columns, (value's data + 0) as a pointer, value's rows * 16)

to [set UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [vertex buffer] {integer:slot} [from] {a pointer:data} [spanning] {integer:count} [bytes]:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's vertices, nothing, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass, a UI operation integer from slot, data, a UI operation integer from count)

to [set UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [to indices] {a pointer to a 32 bit unsigned integer:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's indices, nothing, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass, data, a UI operation integer from count)

to [set UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [to draws] {a pointer to UI shader draw:data} [counting] {integer:count}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's draws, nothing, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass, data, a UI operation integer from count)

to [set UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [enabled] {boolean:enabled}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's pass state, nothing, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass, a UI operation integer from (1 if enabled, else 0))

to get [the byte count of UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [buffer] {integer:slot} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    return @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's buffer bytes, an integer, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass, a UI operation integer from slot)

to get [the record count of UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [buffer] {integer:slot} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    return @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's buffer records, an integer, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass, a UI operation integer from slot)

to get [the index count of UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [pass] {integer:pass} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    return @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's index count, an integer, view, shader, a UI operation integer from pass)

to [close UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's close, nothing, view, shader)

to [set UI shader] {a pointer:shader} [image] {a value:name} [in] {a pointer to UI view:view} [level] {integer:level} [layer] {integer:layer} [from] {a pointer:data} [spanning] {integer:count} [bytes]:
    set provider to the UI shader operations in view
    set title to the string form of name
    require condition (title's length > 0) reporting "Shader image uploads require a resource name"
    @intrinsic("call pointer", provider's images, nothing, view, shader, (the data of title) as a pointer, a UI operation integer from (title's length), a UI operation integer from level, a UI operation integer from layer, data, a UI operation integer from count)
